      "content": "The committee is already pretty skittish about the XJ-9 budget given the recent market shifts. If I tell them there's even moderate volatility or uncertainty in the efficacy projections, they're likely to freeze the next round of funding until we finish the full Phase III, which we can't afford to do without this allocation. \n\nCan you be more specific? When you say \"high degree of confidence,\" what does that actually look like in terms of a statistical certainty? And how much of that \"noise\" in the secondary markers is actually impacting the reliability of the primary efficacy prediction?",
